[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: ETSI-OS-5-3_SecurityProfiles
TITLE: Security profiles

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: General

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This clause specifies, normatively, the mitigations a product shall implement. There are two security profiles, SP-REST and SP-GEN, one for each basic use case in clause 4.7.2. A product is assigned the security profile of its basic use case, determined as in clause 4.7.4.

A product shall implement:

* every baseline mitigation listed for its security profile, in clause 5.3.2 for SP-REST or clause 5.3.3 for SP-GEN; and

* every conditioned mitigation in clause 5.3.4 whose condition the product meets, whatever the product's security profile.

Overlaps between the baseline and the conditioned mitigations resolve by union: where a conditioned mitigation already appears in the product's baseline, the condition adds nothing further. Where a mitigation also carries an applicability field stated with its requirement in clause 5, that mitigation applies only when the stated condition holds for the product.

Where a list shows alternative mitigations separated by "or", the manufacturer shall implement at least one of the listed alternatives. The selection shall be based on the product's implementation characteristics and capabilities. The manufacturer shall document which alternative was selected and the rationale for the selection, as part of the conformity assessment evidence.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: ETSI-OS-SP-REST
TITLE: SP-REST baseline mitigations

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
A restricted operating system (UC-REST) implements the following mitigations regardless of any condition. They address the known-vulnerability threat to a product that receives updates, and require state of the art cryptography in accordance with Annex K wherever the product uses cryptography; every other mitigation is contributed by a condition in clause 5.3.4:

1) (KEVD or KEVA)

2) KEVM

3) SCUE

4) SUVI

5) SUDP

6) SUAR

7) CRYP
<<<

