- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETSI-OS-MI-CRYP

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: TR-IDST: Integrity of data stored on the product

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETSI-OS-AC-DCST
TITLE: [AC-DCST] Assessment criteria: Detect corruption of stored data
DESCRIPTION: >>>
**Assessment reference**

Mitigation MI-DCST.

**Assessment objective**

Detect corruption of stored data.

**Assessment preparation**

1) List the types of data stored on the product for which the product provides the capability to detect corruption, and the corruption-detection mechanism the manufacturer documents for each.

**Assessment activities**

1) For each type of stored data and its corruption-detection mechanism, enable the mechanism, introduce corruption that it is designed to detect, and verify that the product detects it.

**Assessment verdict**

The verdict fail is assigned if any of the following conditions apply:

1) The product does not provide the capability to detect corruption of at least one type of stored data, or does not detect the introduced corruption.

The verdict pass is assigned if none of the above conditions apply and all of the following conditions are met:

1) The product provides the capability to detect corruption of each type of stored data and detects the introduced corruption.

**Assessment evidence**

1) Documentation of the corruption-detection capability per data type, and results showing detection of introduced corruption.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETSI-OS-MI-DCST

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETSI-OS-AC-INTS
TITLE: [AC-INTS] Assessment criteria: Cryptographic integrity protection of stored data
DESCRIPTION: >>>
**Assessment reference**

Mitigation MI-INTS.

**Assessment objective**

Verify that cryptographic mechanisms used for integrity protection of stored data conform to TR-CRYP.

**Assessment preparation**

1) List the categories of stored data for which the product uses cryptographic integrity mechanisms, and for each the cryptographic mechanism and algorithm documented by the manufacturer.

**Assessment activities**

1) Review the documentation to verify that each cryptographic integrity mechanism used for stored data conforms to TR-CRYP.

2) Inspect the operating system in its operational state and verify that the cryptographic integrity mechanisms in use for stored data match the documentation and conform to TR-CRYP.

**Assessment verdict**

The verdict fail is assigned if any of the following conditions apply:

1) Any cryptographic integrity mechanism used for stored data does not conform to TR-CRYP.

2) A cryptographic integrity mechanism in use for stored data does not match the documentation or does not conform to TR-CRYP.

The verdict pass is assigned if none of the above conditions apply and all of the following conditions are met:

1) Every cryptographic integrity mechanism used for stored data conforms to TR-CRYP.

2) The cryptographic integrity mechanisms in use for stored data match the documentation and conform to TR-CRYP.

**Assessment evidence**

1) Documentation of the cryptographic integrity mechanisms and algorithms used for stored data.

2) Results showing the cryptographic integrity mechanisms in use for stored data and their conformance to TR-CRYP.
<<<
