     - Low
     - SP-REST
   * - all others
     - Medium
     - SP-GEN, C-MOD, C-APPS, C-MULTI
   * - any of NUSR or SWMD is at level 2 and SENF is at level 2
     - High
     - C-APPS or C-MULTI, with C-FUNC

Mitigations for Impact:

* Medium to Low: LOGG, ENST, ACSD, DCST, INTS, SDEL

* High to Low: LOGG, ENST, ACSD, DCST, INTS, SDEL

.. list-table:: Table B.4-10: Impact of TH-UAPS
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 55 15 30

   * - Risk factors
     - Impact
     - Reached by
   * - none of SNDS, SNDT, SENF, or PPII is above level 0
     - Low
     - SP-REST
   * - the highest of SNDS, SNDT, SENF, and PPII is at level 1
     - Medium
     - SP-GEN, C-DATA
   * - SENF is at level 2
     - High
     - C-FUNC
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: ETSI-OS-TH-UAPN
LEVEL: B.4.7
TITLE: TH-UAPN: Unauthorised access to product assets via unprotected network interfaces in default configuration

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Attacker can use unprotected debug or management interfaces to get unauthorised access to product assets via the network in the default configuration of the product.

Assets affected: Network assets, Data assets, and Identity and access assets.

Requirements that mitigate this threat: TR-SDEF, TR-AUTH, TR-LOGG, TR-CDST, TR-IDST, TR-SCDL

Mitigations for Likelihood:

* Medium to Low: PDDI-1, AUTH-1, AUTH-2, LCKT, CRED

* High to Low: ADEF, PDDI-3, AUTH-1, AUTH-2, LCKT, CRED, ACCS, SESS

