[[SECTION]]
UID: ETSI-OS-TH-RDPS
LEVEL: B.4.15
TITLE: TH-RDPS: Compromise of the remote data processing solution boundary

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Attacker can compromise the boundary between the product and a remote data processing solution by impersonating the remote endpoint, or by disrupting availability of interactions exchanged across the boundary, affecting the behaviour, state, configuration, or security of the RDPS-dependent product function described in clause 4.8.

Assets affected: Network assets, Data assets, Identity and access assets, and Product functions.

Requirements that mitigate this threat: TR-AUTH, TR-AVAI, TR-CRYP, TR-CDTX, TR-IDTX, TR-LOGG

Mitigations for Likelihood:

* Medium to Low: RAUT, CRYP, CDTX, ENTX, INTT

